{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks to Brilliant.org for supporting PBS Digital Studios"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 4080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Black Holes are really only dangerous if you get too close"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 7920,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Who am I kidding ?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 8980,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It turns out that they may be responsible for ending Star formation across the entire Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19260,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we first realized that Black Holes could have masses of Millions"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23580,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or even Billions of times that of the Sun"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26060,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It came as a bit of a shock"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 27920,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were discovered as the driving force behind Quasars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 31680,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where matter is heated to extreme \nIncandescence"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35480,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "before it plunges into vast Black Holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38900,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if that weren't enough we soon realized that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42180,
    "dDurationMs": 5460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "every single decent sized Galaxy contains such a Supermassive Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47820,
    "dDurationMs": 2420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While in the beginning of the Twenty-first Century"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50400,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it became clear that Black Holes and the Galaxies that contain them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 54460,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are very closely connected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55820,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Bigger the Galaxy, The Bigger Supermassive Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59240,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that might not sound surprising"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61400,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but what was weird was how closely they were connected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64780,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there's a tight co-relation between the mass of the Central Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68540,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the mass of the star in the galactic bulge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71260,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's the central bowl like part of a spiral galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 74500,
    "dDurationMs": 2500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the entirety of an Elliptical galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 77020,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and every bulge contains a Supermassive Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80560,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 1/1000th of its mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83260,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and there's an even tighter relationship between the Black Hole mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87640,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and the speed that stars are moving in their random orbits within galactic bulge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92580,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the so called, Stellar Velocity Dispersion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 95620,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which itself depends on the total mass of the Galaxy including Dark Matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99880,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so why shouldn't a Galaxy and its Black Hole be closely connected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103800,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A couple of things you need to know"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 106220,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even though Supermassive Black Holes are Big"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109400,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they're peanuts compared to the Galaxies they live in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113040,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their Gravitational influence should only extend to the stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 116920,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right at the very centre of the galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 118620,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they definitely aren't directly responsible for the speed of stellar orbits"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123060,
    "dDurationMs": 1720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outside their local region"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124780,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Sure, Galaxies and their Black Holes probably grew together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128900,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but galaxy formation is an extremely messy process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132400,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so you'd expected a huge amount of variation in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135880,
    "dDurationMs": 1760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Black Hole vs. Galaxy mass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138000,
    "dDurationMs": 1080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Because of all of this,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139300,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the tightness of the Black Hole-Galaxy connection"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 142860,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been a decades-long conundrum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145300,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that still is not solved"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 147860,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But one of the leading ideas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149800,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is that Central Black Holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151420,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somehow extend their nefarious influence throughout the entire Galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156560,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "disrupting its ability to grow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 158820,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160280,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We first need to understand how galaxies formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 163360,
    "dDurationMs": 640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in short,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164620,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Small Galaxies collapse from the gas of Big Bang"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167820,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then they smash together to make bigger galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170540,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is 'Bottom up Hierarchical galaxy formation'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174120,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As opposed to 'Top-down'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176080,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which would have the large galaxies collapsing directly from the gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180040,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, Based on our understanding of Physics of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182760,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "especially the nature of Dark Matter and Dark Energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185900,
    "dDurationMs": 2260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we expect 'Bottom up Galaxy formation'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188160,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is what we see in our simulations of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 191600,
    "dDurationMs": 4600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and also mostly agrees with what we see when we look out into the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 196200,
    "dDurationMs": 2940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so galaxies first grew in clusters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 199200,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the densest parts of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201520,
    "dDurationMs": 2620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Places where enormous worlds of Dark Matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 204140,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "pulled in great rivers of material from all around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206940,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gas poured into the clusters from outside of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 210420,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "igniting bouts of extreme star formation called Star Busts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214460,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as galaxies grew so did their Black Holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217180,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would've started as a ready mass of seed Black Holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220120,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "formed by the very first generation of stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 222880,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they would fall to the centres of their local wispy protor galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 226140,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when wisps merged their central Black Holes would also merge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 231380,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all the while gorging on the rich gas supply in the early Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236060,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, Black Holes grew as Galaxies grew."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239560,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then why is it so surprising that they appear so closely correlated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 244040,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the Modern Universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245640,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two Things:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 246760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In order for the Black Hole to grow in lock step with the galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250920,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you need to get a consistent proportion of new material"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254500,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "down into the centre of the Galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256820,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That's challenging, given how messy and varied"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259940,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the whole galaxy assembly process seems to be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 262760,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Second"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264060,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Observation seem to indicate that early Black Holes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 267580,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually grew faster than their surrounding galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 270560,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The 'Galaxy Black Hole Mass Relationships' seem to evolve"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275060,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the history of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276760,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "many Supermassive Black Holes were in place early"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 280360,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving the surrounding galaxies to catch up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 283340,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like a puppy growing into its giant feet"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 286240,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in fact we've seen quasars shining out from less than a Billion years after the Big bang"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 291120,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with masses of 10 Billion suns"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293300,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Easily as large as the largest in the modern Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 297180,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if Black Holes and Galaxies are not growing in lock step with each other"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 302280,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the same material"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303800,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they can't directly influence each other with gravity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307220,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how do they know what size to be?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309460,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "how does a galaxy know to stop growing when its 1000 times larger"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313160,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "than the Central Black Hole?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 314600,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "perhaps the best contender is that the black holes kill galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319080,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and by \"kill\" , I mean make them dead"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321400,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which I guess is the usual sense of the word Kill."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 324860,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in Astronomy, a dead galaxy refers to its current star formation activity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330540,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in particular, the largest galaxies in the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333860,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are the Giant Elliptical's"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 335220,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and we say they are 'Red and Dead'"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337380,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not because they contain lots of old west themed planets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 340720,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that's not yet known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 342460,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but rather, its because they appeared to have almost no active star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346460,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and haven't had any for long time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 348640,
    "dDurationMs": 4580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The short-lived hot massive stars that give Spiral galaxies, like the Milky way,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353220,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "their blue-white sheen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 354900,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have long since died out in giant ellipticals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358180,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving them tinged with the orange-red colours of longer lived cooler stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 362940,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but from what we can tell those giant galaxies should've kept forming stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368200,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Giant reservoirs of gas flowed into those clusters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371340,
    "dDurationMs": 1620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the outside Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373100,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In our simulations of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 375220,
    "dDurationMs": 2900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clustered ellipticals end up much bigger and bluer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378120,
    "dDurationMs": 3180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Due to Billions of more years of ongoing star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 381420,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A likely culprit is the Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 384420,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it kills star formation in those giant galaxies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387660,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fixing the maximum size they could grow"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390880,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the process is called 'Quenching'."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393280,
    "dDurationMs": 3300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are couple different ways it can happen via Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397160,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but all of them involve a Quasar switching on and blasting the crap"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401640,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out of the galaxy's gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403160,
    "dDurationMs": 2700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rewinding a bit to the whole galaxy formation thing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 405860,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when galaxies collide or even get stirred up a bit by eating a smaller galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410420,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gas tends to get driven down to the center where its gobbled up by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414680,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416300,
    "dDurationMs": 1180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, some of it is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 417480,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "close to the Black Hole the gas forms a whirlpool-like accretion disk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 421420,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "heated by the energy that's long formed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423940,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it gets so hot that around 10% the mass of the infalling gas is converted to energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 428840,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the form of light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430440,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and yet more of the gas is blasted outwards by"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433040,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that same light"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 433880,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in colossal winds that rip through the surrounding galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437840,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or its channeled into jets by powerful magnetic fields."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 441500,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A Quasars's intense brightness and its powerful winds and jets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445120,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "can dump an enormous amount of energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 447380,
    "dDurationMs": 2060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into the gas through the surrounding galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449960,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that can do two things"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 451400,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It can drive gas out of the galaxy and prevent new gas arriving"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455240,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or it can heat the gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457460,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "either case is bad for star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459720,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the later case is because hot gas can't form new stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463600,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "gas has to cool down before the force of gravity  can cause it to collapse into the stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 468840,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "too hot and it stays puffed up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 470280,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as well as killing star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472680,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "quasar activity limits the Black Hole's own growth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476480,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it grows relating the new supply of gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 479040,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then its energy output stops new gas falling into the Galactic centre"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 483920,
    "dDurationMs": 2140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in the end you have this balancing act"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486440,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a feedback process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 487720,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more massive the galaxy, the more stuff it can pull in to feed itself in the Black Hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492080,
    "dDurationMs": 5180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but the more mass of the Black hole, the better it is at shutting down the star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 497480,
    "dDurationMs": 1280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and its own feeding"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 498760,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the end result is that Black Hole mass and Galaxy size"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 502280,
    "dDurationMs": 1320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are closely linked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503600,
    "dDurationMs": 3220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and in the largest galaxies our red dead ellipticals"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 506960,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "star formation is entirely shut down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509920,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whether or not black holes kill star formation or at least were the main culprit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 515060,
    "dDurationMs": 1660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is not established"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 516820,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but we do know that the star formation died"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 520240,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or is dying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 521720,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "not just in largest galaxies but across the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 524320,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "after the first stars formed around 150 million years after the big bang"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 528840,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rate of star formation across the Universe slowly rose"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533200,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it became concentrated in the most denser region of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 536740,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "where giant ellipticals assembled"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539140,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the rising storm of star formation reached a crescendo around"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 543180,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "8 to 10 Billions years ago and remain intense for few Billion years"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547460,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "following that the work of star formation shifted towards the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 551440,
    "dDurationMs": 2860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "outer regions further from the giant clusters"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554500,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the past several Billion years the cosmic star formation rate"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558860,
    "dDurationMs": 1200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "has been dropping"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 560280,
    "dDurationMs": 1440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and continues to do so"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561720,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this is mainly due to star formation shutting down in the densest parts of the Universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 566640,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which as I mentioned is strange"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 569040,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "given i should still have plenty of gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 572020,
    "dDurationMs": 4540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there are other explanations besides quasars and Black Holes for the shut down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 576680,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "star formation has to be a somewhat self-limiting process because"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 581600,
    "dDurationMs": 4180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "intense starbursts leads to intense supernova activity"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585920,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which could also heat or expell gas and limit further formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590860,
    "dDurationMs": 2740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the largest galaxies the shock experience"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593600,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by gas falling in from the outside universe can be enough to stop stars forming"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598640,
    "dDurationMs": 3620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "all of these probably play some role in killing star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 602300,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are accomplices to the crime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 604640,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but many astronomers think Supermassive Black holes are the main suspect"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 609740,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "here's one final clue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612260,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "compare the cosmic history of black hole growth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615460,
    "dDurationMs": 1460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to that of star formation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616980,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they grow together and peak at the same time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 620700,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around 10 Billion years ago"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622940,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right before star formation begins to die"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 626160,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now some very massive black holes existed earlier than this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 630340,
    "dDurationMs": 1600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "somewhat perplexingly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 632040,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but this peak in black hole growth represents the peak of the quasar epoch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 636700,
    "dDurationMs": 5240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "when the most outrageously luminous quasars shone from the most"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641940,
    "dDurationMs": 1900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ridiculously massive galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 644420,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Surely enough to shut down those galaxies' further growth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 649040,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the modern universe Giant Dead galaxies harbor"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652980,
    "dDurationMs": 900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "fossil quasars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 654420,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "supermassive Black Holes whose close connection to their surrounding galaxy is a clue"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660460,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "incriminating evidence suggest a long and violent struggle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 664500,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a feedback cycle of growth and quenching"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 667460,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that neither quasar nor star forming galaxy would survive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672300,
    "dDurationMs": 4500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and perhaps for the best - for the comfort of the life bearing world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677080,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to leave raging starbursts and fiery quasars to an earlier epoch"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 682080,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of Space-Time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 684000,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Learning astrophysics is tough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686160,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "thankfully there are online tools that can help"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 688000,
    "dDurationMs": 3060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like Brilliant a problem solving website that teaches you to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 691060,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "tackle difficult topics and think like a scientist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693940,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By breaking up complexities into understandable pieces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 697280,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and instead of just passively listening to lectures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700120,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you get to master concepts by solving interesting and challenging problems"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 704880,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so whether you wanna learn about special relativity, quantum physics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 708380,
    "dDurationMs": 3540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or brush up on your complex algebra and differential equations"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 711920,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can learn more at Brilliant.org/spacetime"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 716420,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Last time we talked about all the cool elements that get made when neutron stars collide."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 721320,
    "dDurationMs": 660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Your comments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722380,
    "dDurationMs": 920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "were gold."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 724040,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A number of people wondered whether the Fermi Paradox"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726600,
    "dDurationMs": 3960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "might be explained by the fact that neutron star collisions are rare"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 730820,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that only lucky parts of the galaxies have"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732840,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a high abundance of the products of those collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 736200,
    "dDurationMs": 800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actually..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737400,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "although these collisions are rare"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 739280,
    "dDurationMs": 1060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are common enough"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740720,
    "dDurationMs": 2560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that most of the galaxy gets a decent amount"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743280,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of all the stable products of neutron star collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746880,
    "dDurationMs": 680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "On the other hand,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 747560,
    "dDurationMs": 2540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the presence of highly radioactive stuff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 750100,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with very short half-lives"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 752100,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a telltale sign of recent merger."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 755180,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, that stuff probably isn't essential to life."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759300,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Speaking of half-lives, Anthony Schroeder picked up a silly mistake"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 763280,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I said that the half-life is the average decay time of a radioactive element"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 768060,
    "dDurationMs": 660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 769000,
    "dDurationMs": 3340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's the amount of time for half of the given sample to decay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 772800,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that's not the same as the average."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 775040,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact, it's longer by around 44%"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777260,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or one over the natural log of 2"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779860,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Thanks Anthony, I guess I need to retake nuclear physics."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784440,
    "dDurationMs": 5880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tricky asks us why we don't see more strange matter from neutron star collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790840,
    "dDurationMs": 1340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, this is a cool point."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792620,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It may be that some neutron stars are actually \"Strange Stars\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 796440,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whose nuclear material is composed of strange matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 800100,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means up, down, and strange quarks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 804180,
    "dDurationMs": 2100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If such a star was disrupted,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 806280,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "then we would expect to see blobs of strange matter in the debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 810100,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the thing is, strange matter is probably only stable under extreme pressure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814780,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Release it from the embrace of the neutron star"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817540,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all the strange quarks probably decay into boring old up and down quarks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822300,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which would join together to become protons and neutrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825000,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which means you are back to where you started from."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827760,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Even if strange matter is stable as so called \"Strangelets\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832100,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are electrically neutral, so they don't have an electromagnetic signature."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 836580,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "By the way, you wouldn't actually \"see\" strange matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840660,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But you might see the result of it's decay"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 843280,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a particular spectrum of radiation and cosmic rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 847500,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or in the detailed shape of the gravitational wave signal before collision."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 851760,
    "dDurationMs": 1020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "People are looking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 853600,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Nadira Rahman notices that their cat loves the sound of my voice"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 857380,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and moves closer the the screen every time"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 860460,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually that's just because Mittens can sense my allergy and like all cats"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865960,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is drawn to my suffering."
    } ]
  } ]
}
